## Reference Implementation: Tickets Feature API

| Method | Endpoint | Specific Enforcement Pattern |
| ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |
| GET | `/api/tickets` | `search` = title+desc ILIKE; invalid `status` filter → 400 |
| POST | `/api/tickets` | Status auto-set to Open; `createdBy` required valid user ID |
| PATCH | `/api/tickets/:id` | **Reject `status` field → 400 `STATUS_NOT_ALLOWED_HERE`** |
| PATCH | `/api/tickets/:id/status` | Validate transition via `statusTransition.ts`; 400 on failure |
| GET | `/api/tickets/:id` | Returns populated relation names: `createdByName`, `assignedToName`, `comments[]` ASC |
| POST | `/api/tickets/:id/comments` | Parent ticket validation; `createdBy` required valid user ID |


## Database

- Schema: `users`, `tickets`, `comments`; enums `Role`, `Priority`, `Status`
- `ON DELETE RESTRICT` on all user FKs
- Migrations incremental — one logical change per migration; never edit applied migrations
- Seed: 3 users (Agent, Manager, Admin); ≥5 tickets across all 5 statuses; ≥5 comments
- Enum display mapping: `"In Progress"` (API JSON) ↔ `InProgress` (Prisma enum)

## Error Codes

`VALIDATION_ERROR` · `INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION` · `STATUS_NOT_ALLOWED_HERE` · `INVALID_FILTER` · `NOT_FOUND` · `INTERNAL_ERROR`

Never expose Prisma errors or stack traces to API consumers.

## Security

- Validate all inputs server-side — Prisma parameterized queries only
- CORS restricted to `CLIENT_URL` env var
- Never log `DATABASE_URL`, passwords, or credentials
- `.env` gitignored; only `.env.example` with placeholders committed
- No authentication in v1 — document as known limitation, do not work around it
